<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="SPAN 248" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/SPAN/248.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="SPAN" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/SPAN.xml">Spanish</subject></parents><label>Latin American Diaspora through Film: Beyond Braceros, Narcos, and Latin Lovers</label><description>Study of the relationships between Latinx and Latin American culture through film, focusing on sociohistorical processes (migrations, assimilation, political struggles, nationalism, globalization). It goes beyond onscreen stereotypes about Latinx and Latin Americans (narcotraffickers, undocumented migrants and Latin lovers) promoting nuanced perspectives on issues affecting Latinas/os and Latin Americans in their relationship with US culture. 40% of the films are Latin American and 60% Latinx (made in the US). Instruction in English. Same as LLS 248.</description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><courseSectionInformation>Same as LLS 248.</courseSectionInformation><sectionDegreeAttributes>Humanities - Lit &amp; Arts, and Cultural Studies - US Minority course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><classScheduleInformation>Students must register for one lecture and one discussion.</classScheduleInformation><genEdCategories><category id="CS"><description>Cultural Studies</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1US">Cultural Studies - US Minority</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category><category id="HUM"><description>Humanities &amp; the Arts</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1LA">Humanities – Lit &amp; Arts</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCatego